WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:07.671 --> 00:00:11.742
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:17.481
Arr, this scalawag be
a right thorn in me side.

00:00:17.481 --> 00:00:18.682
Let it be known that--

00:00:18.682 --> 00:00:24.488
[coughing]

00:00:24.488 --> 00:00:26.657
Eh, okay, that's enough of that.

00:00:26.657 --> 00:00:29.226
I've got another 20 years
and a lot of whiskey drinking

00:00:29.226 --> 00:00:31.328
before my voice sounds
like that normally.

00:00:31.328 --> 00:00:33.764
No more piracy for me.

00:00:33.764 --> 00:00:35.165
So, do I still have problems?

00:00:36.033 --> 00:00:37.267
I still have problems.

00:00:38.602 --> 00:00:41.572
This sounds like a job for
Ambassador Pineapple.

00:00:41.572 --> 00:00:43.707
You'll be representing me on the floor.

00:00:43.707 --> 00:00:45.809
Now, go out there and work your magic.

00:00:47.077 --> 00:00:48.445
[explosion]

00:00:48.445 --> 00:00:51.048
Oh, sounds like we came to a resolution.

00:00:51.782 --> 00:00:53.784
Testing, one-two?

00:00:53.784 --> 00:00:54.818
Testing.

00:00:55.719 --> 00:00:58.088
Well, I'm glad everything worked out.

00:00:59.723 --> 00:01:01.091
So, what's this?

00:01:01.091 --> 00:01:01.959
"Surrender..."

00:01:01.959 --> 00:01:03.894
Oh, shit!

00:01:03.894 --> 00:01:06.096
They know my name!

00:01:06.096 --> 00:01:08.465
Fuuuuuck!

00:01:08.465 --> 00:01:10.634
This changes everything.

00:01:10.634 --> 00:01:14.271
I can't just waltz out of here now;
I'm wanted!

00:01:14.271 --> 00:01:17.107
Dammit. My beard betrayed me!

00:01:17.107 --> 00:01:20.978
They got an ID because I'm the only
fucking scientist here with a beard.

00:01:20.978 --> 00:01:23.113
If I'd gone with that
stupid Einstein hair,

00:01:23.113 --> 00:01:25.182
they wouldn't be able to
pick me out from a lineup.

00:01:25.182 --> 00:01:27.851
Okay, focus, focus.

00:01:27.851 --> 00:01:30.120
The first objective is to not die.

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:31.855
That hasn't changed.

00:01:31.855 --> 00:01:35.659
The second is...to not...
detonate this missile, I guess.

00:01:35.659 --> 00:01:36.560
HECU: Okay, mission...

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:39.196
Ah!  God!  Damn!  Jesus!  Fuck!

00:01:39.196 --> 00:01:41.732
Yeah, I guess nothing's
really changed, has it?

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:46.370
You dumb bastards.

00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:49.573
This is the WRONG PLACE to lay an ambush.

00:01:49.573 --> 00:01:51.875
You don't set explosive tripmines down

00:01:51.875 --> 00:01:55.779
then start firing automatic weapons
next to a missile, all right?

00:01:55.779 --> 00:01:59.783
I understand you guys have hostility
issues or whatever and want to kill me,

00:01:59.783 --> 00:02:03.520
but regardless, I would think
that weapons are the one thing

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:05.789
you jarheads might understand
something about.

00:02:05.789 --> 00:02:07.057
[metal groaning]

00:02:07.057 --> 00:02:09.760
That's not a good sound.

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:10.861
I'm leaving.

00:02:11.862 --> 00:02:15.032
This is suspiciously convenient.

00:02:15.032 --> 00:02:19.803
I haven't been used to things
going my way for quite a while now.

00:02:19.803 --> 00:02:22.806
Hey, hey, maybe it's karmic balance.

00:02:22.806 --> 00:02:25.976
Since now I know I have much
bigger long-term problems,

00:02:25.976 --> 00:02:28.178
I'll have less short-term ones.

00:02:29.246 --> 00:02:33.183
No, lasers, aliens, I just
flat-out have problems.

00:02:33.183 --> 00:02:35.719
But I'm willing to share my problems.

00:02:39.189 --> 00:02:41.625
See?  Now we all have problems.

00:02:41.625 --> 00:02:43.460
I really do have problems, though.

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:44.628
Oh, hey, a door.

00:02:44.628 --> 00:02:46.863
Stop, stop, I command you.

00:02:48.165 --> 00:02:48.699
Okay.

00:02:49.533 --> 00:02:51.835
There's got to be some money in
one of these rooms.

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:55.138
No, this is the wrong one.

00:02:55.906 --> 00:02:58.108
Ah, thought you were sneaky, huh?

00:02:58.108 --> 00:03:01.278
What the hell?  Did it just shut
the door on me?

00:03:01.278 --> 00:03:03.180
But I'm a great salesman!

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:05.649
Hi!  I'm selling these fine used bullets.

00:03:05.649 --> 00:03:07.017
Free samples.

00:03:07.017 --> 00:03:10.020
Oh, it looks like you already have some,
from the looks of things.

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:10.854
But then why is there no--

00:03:10.854 --> 00:03:12.089
[headcrab squeals]

00:03:12.089 --> 00:03:13.490
Ah, the missus of the house!

00:03:13.490 --> 00:03:14.958
Try some of our product.

00:03:15.659 --> 00:03:17.561
This sale isn't going very well.

00:03:17.561 --> 00:03:19.396
I'm just going to grab
the ammo and leave.

00:03:19.396 --> 00:03:21.665
It smells like a vomitorium in here.

00:03:21.665 --> 00:03:24.101
Makes you wonder what the
purpose of this room was.

00:03:24.101 --> 00:03:26.403
I'm not even seeing a storage crate.

00:03:26.403 --> 00:03:27.671
What's this?

00:03:27.671 --> 00:03:29.573
"Yore Dead".

00:03:29.573 --> 00:03:30.207
Wow.

00:03:30.607 --> 00:03:32.776
I can't even make fun of that.

00:03:32.776 --> 00:03:36.046
Military intelligence aside, how
did they know I was going to be here?

00:03:36.046 --> 00:03:37.114
This is a dead end.

00:03:37.581 --> 00:03:39.983
Okay, that's it.
No more side-paths.

00:03:39.983 --> 00:03:42.252
It's not like I know where I'm
going anyway,

00:03:42.252 --> 00:03:45.889
but that security guy said I could take
this track straight to the surface.

00:03:45.889 --> 00:03:47.858
Now, I do know he's a liar,

00:03:47.858 --> 00:03:50.594
but so far, he's said things
that have been half-true.

00:03:50.594 --> 00:03:52.062
Y'know, like the Devil.

00:03:52.062 --> 00:03:56.500
So, statistically, it makes more
sense to follow the advice of a half-liar,

00:03:56.500 --> 00:03:59.536
versus making completely random
decisions like I have been.

00:03:59.536 --> 00:04:00.203
What is that?

00:04:00.804 --> 00:04:02.439
JESUS CHRIST!

00:04:02.439 --> 00:04:04.141
NEXT STOP: RIGHT HERE!

00:04:04.141 --> 00:04:05.509
YOU CAN HAVE THE TRAM!

00:04:05.509 --> 00:04:06.243
FUCK!

00:04:06.243 --> 00:04:07.911
You just wrecked my train of thought.

00:04:07.911 --> 00:04:09.980
Uh, I should turn my light off.

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:12.048
So, uh, are we cool now?

00:04:13.083 --> 00:04:14.718
I don't think he sees me.

00:04:14.718 --> 00:04:15.952
That's good, but I--OH!

00:04:18.989 --> 00:04:20.357
I don't like how liberal this guy is

00:04:20.357 --> 00:04:23.193
about firing rockets
inside an underground tunnel.

00:04:23.193 --> 00:04:25.562
He's playing Chicken Little and
doesn't even know it.

00:04:28.365 --> 00:04:30.634
I don't think this guy's got an
architectural, engineering,

00:04:30.634 --> 00:04:34.371
or even a geology degree to accurately
assess the load-bearing stress of rock

00:04:34.371 --> 00:04:35.505
that's on this tunnel.

00:04:39.209 --> 00:04:41.077
Rocky the rocket ranger....

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:43.947
God!

00:04:44.581 --> 00:04:47.818
You see, I have to kill you
before you kill yourself!

00:04:48.185 --> 00:04:49.085
And me!

00:04:51.922 --> 00:04:54.858
Well, either that's a hit or
he's a very good actor.

00:04:54.858 --> 00:04:58.228
As long as he stays down, I don't
think I need to do a confirmation kill.

00:04:58.228 --> 00:05:00.564
I'm not at that phase in my life yet.

00:05:00.564 --> 00:05:03.200
Okay, so how do I operate this thing?

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:04.701
I want to blow things up, too.

00:05:05.402 --> 00:05:07.237
Oh, I think it's out of rockets.

00:05:08.505 --> 00:05:10.841
Oh well, guess I'm walking now.

00:05:11.708 --> 00:05:13.777
God-damned rocket launcher....

00:05:13.777 --> 00:05:17.147
You know, everyone's always told me
that I'm paranoid and I need to calm down.

00:05:17.147 --> 00:05:18.014
But guess what?

00:05:18.315 --> 00:05:19.616
I'm alive.

00:05:19.616 --> 00:05:21.952
And everyone who said that is dead.

00:05:21.952 --> 00:05:23.787
That's the ultimate proof that
someone doesn't know

00:05:23.787 --> 00:05:25.522
what the hell they're talking about.

00:05:25.522 --> 00:05:28.959
"Follow my advice and you'll die
just like me!  Huh-heh!"

00:05:29.526 --> 00:05:32.529
I have the US Military spray
painting my name on a wall,

00:05:32.529 --> 00:05:33.697
setting laser traps,

00:05:33.697 --> 00:05:35.866
and firing a fucking
rocket launcher at me,

00:05:35.866 --> 00:05:38.802
and people have the gall to
call me paranoid.

00:05:38.802 --> 00:05:39.703
Fuck them!

00:05:39.703 --> 00:05:41.004
Fuck everybody!

00:05:41.004 --> 00:05:44.174
Anyone who doesn't listen to me
deserves the fate they get!

00:05:44.174 --> 00:05:46.243
I should kill everyone just on principle!

00:05:47.911 --> 00:05:49.713
See, this is what I'm talking about!

00:05:51.081 --> 00:05:54.150
"Aliens aren't invading, Freeman.
You're just being paranoid."

00:05:55.252 --> 00:05:58.522
"The mailman's not spying on you,
Freeman. You're just being paranoid."

00:06:00.357 --> 00:06:01.224
What else?

00:06:02.659 --> 00:06:06.463
"There's no society of anthropomorphic
frog people living in the sewer, Freeman.

00:06:06.463 --> 00:06:07.964
"You're just being paranoid."

00:06:09.299 --> 00:06:13.136
"Owls can't read your thoughts, Freeman.
You're just being paranoid."

00:06:15.205 --> 00:06:18.408
Bet you wouldn't call me paranoid
now if you were still alive.

00:06:18.408 --> 00:06:21.945
How about expecting five monsters
to ambush me, is that paranoid?

00:06:21.945 --> 00:06:24.214
Oh, hey, that's nice, the tram
stopped automatically.

00:06:25.048 --> 00:06:28.852
Well, I'm not seeing any controls, but
if this can ram a concrete divider,

00:06:28.852 --> 00:06:31.288
then I'm sure it can handle a
simple wooden gate.

00:06:31.288 --> 00:06:32.722
I am unstoppable.

00:06:34.958 --> 00:06:36.226
Oh, what the hell?

00:06:37.494 --> 00:06:40.230
Something's tripping the
brakes automatically.

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:41.698
Piece of crap.

00:06:41.698 --> 00:06:42.532
Can I move this?

00:06:43.433 --> 00:06:45.235
No, it's locked in there.

00:06:45.235 --> 00:06:48.038
Well, I-- no, wait, wait, wait.

00:06:48.038 --> 00:06:50.440
I bet the controls are down that hallway

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:53.777
and there are a truckload of
soldiers waiting to shoot me.

00:06:53.777 --> 00:06:55.946
I've done this dance before.

00:06:55.946 --> 00:06:58.315
They can keep the damned tram.

00:06:58.315 --> 00:07:00.550
I'm really not that attached to it.

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:03.053
I'm not like those
Jabba the Hutt bastards

00:07:03.053 --> 00:07:06.222
I see in Walmart scooting around
in their motorized carts.

00:07:06.623 --> 00:07:08.091
I can walk.

00:07:08.091 --> 00:07:09.793
And seeing how these clowns operate,

00:07:09.793 --> 00:07:13.964
I'm sure that concept alone is
going to thwart their plans for a while.

00:07:13.964 --> 00:07:17.100
I just hope they don't figure out that
laser tripmines are more effective

00:07:17.100 --> 00:07:19.002
when you can't see the beam.

00:07:19.002 --> 00:07:20.270
That could cause me some problems.

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:23.106
HECU: Echo mission is go.

00:07:23.106 --> 00:07:25.208
Oh, look who called it.

00:07:25.208 --> 00:07:29.112
I think I've just saved myself
and a lot of other people some trouble.

00:07:29.112 --> 00:07:30.146
Let's see.

00:07:31.181 --> 00:07:33.817
Oh, yeah, there he is.

00:07:33.817 --> 00:07:35.485
He doesn't even see me.

00:07:35.485 --> 00:07:37.821
HECU: Okay, control.

00:07:37.821 --> 00:07:39.389
Yeah, look at him.

00:07:39.389 --> 00:07:42.559
He is expecting me from that doorway.

00:07:42.559 --> 00:07:44.294
Glad I didn't go that way.

00:07:44.294 --> 00:07:46.563
So, wait, did I see another tram?

00:07:46.563 --> 00:07:48.031
I did.

00:07:48.031 --> 00:07:49.132
Where's this one go?

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:52.302
Ah, another gate.

00:07:52.302 --> 00:07:54.104
So, the noise would alert this guy,

00:07:54.104 --> 00:07:56.840
and I'd have a grand
journey of about 30 feet.

00:07:56.840 --> 00:07:57.841
I don't think so.

00:07:58.508 --> 00:08:02.212
Hm, I really am bummed that
they've identified me, though.

00:08:02.212 --> 00:08:04.147
That means I'm a fugitive now.

00:08:04.147 --> 00:08:06.616
So, they've probably
frozen my bank accounts.

00:08:06.616 --> 00:08:08.785
I need to get back to
Massachusetts.

00:08:08.785 --> 00:08:13.156
I have about $10,000 in gold buried
in Harold Parker State Forest

00:08:13.156 --> 00:08:16.793
that I put I there for exactly
this kind of situation.

00:08:16.793 --> 00:08:20.430
Now, I didn't anticipate I was
going to get framed like this.

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:22.766
I put it there so in case I got
caught embezzling,

00:08:22.766 --> 00:08:24.968
I would have some sort of exit strategy.

00:08:24.968 --> 00:08:28.271
Now, granted, $10,000 will
only get me so far here.

00:08:28.271 --> 00:08:32.542
But if I can make it to India, I can live
like a king with that kind of money.

00:08:32.542 --> 00:08:35.178
The American dollar goes a
lot farther over there.

00:08:35.178 --> 00:08:38.782
Maim apane na'e bhagavana hum.
Mere se pahale ghutane.

00:08:38.782 --> 00:08:40.717
I'm going to need a fake ID.

00:08:40.717 --> 00:08:43.019
I'll check in with Eddie once I
get out of here.

00:08:43.019 --> 00:08:44.988
He can probably hook something up for me.

00:08:44.988 --> 00:08:48.058
I'm going to need a car, too,
but that shouldn't be too difficult.

00:08:48.158 --> 00:08:50.627
I can just take some motorist
hostage with my machine gun

00:08:50.627 --> 00:08:52.295
and drive to Massachusetts that way.

00:08:52.829 --> 00:08:54.230
Going to be a long drive.

00:08:54.330 --> 00:08:55.732
HECU: Secure, sir.

00:08:55.732 --> 00:08:56.833
Hm, I hear soldiers.

00:08:56.833 --> 00:08:58.101
I'm not stopping here.

00:08:58.101 --> 00:09:00.637
And look, there's another
gate with no switch.

00:09:00.637 --> 00:09:03.306
So, there really was no point to
taking the--OH GOD!

00:09:03.306 --> 00:09:05.742
[groaning, crying out]

00:09:05.742 --> 00:09:07.177
Good, stay!

00:09:07.177 --> 00:09:10.547
That sounds like a heavier caliber gun,
and, while I admit I'm curious,

00:09:10.547 --> 00:09:13.750
I really don't feel like another
bullet-resistance test for this suit.

00:09:13.750 --> 00:09:14.751
Ah-hah!

00:09:14.751 --> 00:09:15.919
Elevator!

00:09:15.919 --> 00:09:16.653
Yes!

00:09:16.653 --> 00:09:19.589
[humming the conga]

00:09:19.589 --> 00:09:22.592
Oh, my God, it goes up and it
doesn't even snap!

00:09:22.592 --> 00:09:23.760
This is amazing!

00:09:25.962 --> 00:09:26.629
What?

00:09:27.931 --> 00:09:29.199
Explosives.

00:09:29.699 --> 00:09:30.300
Oh.

00:09:32.035 --> 00:09:34.003
I should think about this for a minute.

00:09:37.474 --> 00:09:40.210
You know, I'm really starting to
think maybe this whole thing

00:09:40.210 --> 00:09:41.934
isn't a rescue operation.

